    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26371" root="طبن" body-key="T">
    
      Q. Q. 4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِطْبَأَنَّ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِطْمَأَنَّ</span>; (S, K;) formed
from the latter by substitution [of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">م</span>]. (S in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طمن</span>.) So in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِطْبَأَنَّ قَلْبُهُ</span>, meaning <i>His heart became quiet, at rest, at ease,</i> or
<i>tranquil.</i> (TA.)

